<article class="env-corollary" id="06H0">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06H0">Corollary <span data-tag="06H0">9.4.1.17</span>.</a> Let $\kappa \leq \lambda $ be regular cardinals, let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category which is $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-compactly generated, and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be an $\infty $-category which is $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-cocomplete. Then a functor $G: \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-finitary if and only if it satisfies the following condition: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(\ast )$</dt>
<dd><p>
For every $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-compact object $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the composition 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\xrightarrow {G} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\xrightarrow { \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( C, \bullet ) } \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{&lt; \mu }  \]
</div>
<p>
 is $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-finitary. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
<p> Here $\mu \geq \lambda $ denotes any regular cardinal for which $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is locally $\mu $-small. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{&lt; \kappa } \subseteq \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be the full subcategory of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ spanned by the $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-compact objects. It follows from Propositions <a data-tag="067B" href="/tag/067B">9.4.1.11</a> and <a data-tag="04BQ" href="/tag/04BQ">8.4.6.8</a>, that the restricted Yoneda embedding 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ h_{\bullet }: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}}_{&lt; \kappa }, \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{&lt; \mu } ) \quad \quad X \mapsto \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(\bullet , X) \]
</div>
<p>
       is an equivalence from $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ to the smallest full subcategory of $\operatorname{Fun}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}}_{&lt; \kappa }, \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{&lt; \mu } )$ which contains all representable functors and is closed under $\lambda $-small $\kappa $-filtered colimits. It follows that $G$ is $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-finitary if and only if the composition $h_{\bullet } \circ G$ is $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-finitary. The equivalence of this condition with $(\ast )$ follows from the observation that $\mu $-small colimits in $\operatorname{Fun}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{&lt; \mu } )$ are computed levelwise (Proposition <a data-tag="02X9" href="/tag/02X9">7.1.8.3</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></p></article>
